  "title": "Battle of Omdurman",
  "summary": "On 2 September 1898, an Anglo-Egyptian army under Major General Herbert Kitchener defeated the Mahdist forces of Khalifa Abdullah near Omdurman, Sudan. The battle, fought on the Kerreri plain with modern rifles, Maxim guns, and artillery against spear- and sword-armed Mahdists, broke the Mahdist army.",
